            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski Was there a reason for not using a `%.txt` parent pattern in #29660?\r\n\r\nThere was a reason to extract a separate `require` parent pattern, that essentially boils down to the assumption that \"matching `require` is much less frequent than matching `.txt`\". The rough logic is as follows:\r\n- Assume that files matching `.txt` are at least 10 times more than matching `require`. Let's say, there are 1 file that matches `require` and 10 that match `.txt`.\r\n- With separation `1 parent 'require' with 4 children; 3 fallback '.txt'` the overall pattern matching \"score\" is `(1 + 4 + 3) * 1 + (1 + 3) * 10 = 48`.\r\n- With separation `1 parent '.txt' with 7 children` the overall pattern matching \"score\" is `1 * 1 + (1 + 7) * 10 = 81`. Which is more pattern matching than with a separate `require`.\r\n\r\nThe reason there was/is no separate `%.txt$` pattern for the three fallback patterns that match it is because 3 is a vague threshold (`:h dev-vimpatch-filetype`) where it is more performant to extract in a separate group.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, there is now four patterns that match `%.txt`. So maybe it is worth moving them into a separate parent group, but not together with `require`.\r\n\r\nDid it make sense?",
            "commit_id": "f1da77517e2f98cddf0384445147168e12987bf2",
            "created_at": "2026-09-10T09:20:50Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -2644,6 +2644,40 @@ local pattern = {\n     ['/%.init/.*%.conf$'] = 'upstart',\n     ['/xorg%.conf%.d/.*%.conf$'] = detect.xfree86_v4,\n   },\n+  ['%.txt'] = {",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41797#discussion_r3977523874",
